The `validateFrontendHierarchy` function maps over `handoff?.frontend_ui_hierarchy?.states` without filtering out non-record entries first. Additionally, it does not record an explicit invalid-type diagnostic if the field is present but is not an array.

To ensure the system fails closed gracefully, we should:
1. Filter out non-record entries before mapping.
2. Record an explicit invalid-type diagnostic if the field is present but is not an array.

```javascript
function validateFrontendHierarchy(handoff, errors) {
  if (handoff?.frontend_ui_hierarchy?.states && !Array.isArray(handoff.frontend_ui_hierarchy.states)) {
    errors.push('frontend_ui_hierarchy_states_invalid_type');
  }
  const states = arrayFrom(handoff?.frontend_ui_hierarchy?.states).filter(isRecord);
  const ids = states.map((state) => state.state_id);
  const exactIds = sameArray(ids, REQUIRED_STATE_IDS);
  const refsPresent = states.every((state) => arrayFrom(state.fixture_refs).length > 0);
  if (!exactIds) errors.push('required_frontend_ui_state_ids_missing');
  if (!refsPresent) errors.push('frontend_ui_state_fixture_refs_missing');
  return exactIds && refsPresent;
}
```

