The `buildFixtureCoverage` function maps over `frontendFixtures?.fixtures` and `frontendFixtureManifest?.fixture_manifest` without filtering out non-record entries first. This can lead to potential TypeErrors or unexpected `undefined` values if the collections contain malformed or non-record entries.

To prevent this, we should normalize the input collections and filter out non-record entries before mapping over them.

```suggestion
function buildFixtureCoverage({ paths, frontendFixtures, frontendFixtureManifest }) {
  const fixtures = arrayFrom(frontendFixtures?.fixtures).filter(isRecord);
  const manifestEntries = arrayFrom(frontendFixtureManifest?.fixture_manifest).filter(isRecord);
  const fixtureIds = fixtures.map((fixture) => fixture.fixture_id);
  const manifestIds = manifestEntries.map((entry) => entry.fixture_id);
  return {
    fixture_directory: 'artifacts/method-map/v1-9709',
    fixture_manifest_path: paths.frontendFixtureManifestIn,
    fixture_path: paths.frontendFixturesIn,
    fixture_count: fixtures.length,
    manifest_entry_count: manifestEntries.length,
    required_fixture_ids: REQUIRED_FIXTURE_IDS,
    fixture_ids: fixtureIds,
    manifest_fixture_ids: manifestIds,
  };
}
```

